      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T13:24:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The new WARN_ON() is below, the one we talked about (after the cmpxchg).\n\nI did move this. After checking the patches again and passing it through a review, Gemini noted (and I confirmed) that the original order is load-bearing, not a style choice. Producer is cmpxchg_relaxed(power_state) -\u003e plain writes -\u003e store_release(reset). The cmpxchg is relaxed, so another CPU can observe ON_PENDING (or win ON_PENDING -\u003e ON) before the release on `reset` has propagated.\n\nIf the check is post-cmpxchg, that window leaves power_state \u003d\u003d ON with the reset body skipped, and the next KVM_RUN\u0027s READ_ONCE fast-paths straight into the guest with stale sysregs (and stale PC for the pvmfw primary). Acquire-first costs nothing on a false read, power_state stays at ON_PENDING and the host retries when the release propagates.\n\nAnd not a WARN: that false case is the legitimate release-not-yet-visible window, host-reachable, and an EL2 WARN traps to hyp_panic. The other WARN_ON(prev !\u003d OFF) on the cmpxchg-miss path does stay, because only rollback can produce that prior and the per-CPU loaded_hyp_vcpu cmpxchg keeps the vCPU single-loaded.",
      "parentUuid": "7d0ffbf0_5b2fb82d",
